# Project One Move-Between-Rooms Pseudocode
#
# Graded checkpoint: Module Five Project One
# Later use: conceptual support for M6; movement design for M7
#
# Review the course-provided movement flowchart before completing this file.
# Write pseudocode, not Python code. Use clear indentation and course-appropriate
# keywords such as INPUT, OUTPUT, IF, ELSE, WHILE, SET, or similar terms.

# TODO 1: Identify the information the movement process needs.
# Consider the player's current room and movement command.
SET current_room to "Living room" 
SET direction_input to ""
SET next_room to ""

# TODO 2: Prompt for and receive the player's movement command.
OUTPUT "You are currently in the " + current_room
OUTPUT "Enter a direction to move (north, south, east, west) or type 'exit' to quit: "
INPUT direction_input

# TODO 3: Validate whether the requested movement is possible from the
# current room. Show the decision clearly.
# Based on game_map.drawio connections:
# Living room (east) -> Towel closet
# Towel closet (east) -> Bathroom
# Bathroom (east) -> Cleaning closet, (south) -> Bedroom
# Bedroom (south) -> Laundry room
# Laundry room (south) -> Pantry closet
# Pantry closet (west) -> Kitchen

IF current_room EQUALS "Living room" AND direction_input EQUALS "east" THEN
    SET is_valid_move TO TRUE
    SET next_room TO "Towel closet"
ELSE IF current_room EQUALS "Towel closet" AND direction_input EQUALS "east" THEN
    SET is_valid_move TO TRUE
    SET next_room TO "Bathroom"
ELSE IF current_room EQUALS "Bathroom" AND direction_input EQUALS "east" THEN
    SET is_valid_move TO TRUE
    SET next_room TO "Cleaning closet"
ELSE IF current_room EQUALS "Cleaning closet" AND direction_input EQUALS "west" THEN
    SET is_valid_move TO TRUE
    SET next_room TO "Bathroom"
ELSE IF current_room EQUALS "Bathroom" AND direction_input EQUALS "south" THEN
    SET is_valid_move TO TRUE
    SET next_room TO "Bedroom"
ELSE IF current_room EQUALS "Bedroom" AND direction_input EQUALS "south" THEN
    SET is_valid_move TO TRUE
    SET next_room TO "Laundry room"
ELSE IF current_room EQUALS "Laundry room" AND direction_input EQUALS "south" THEN
    SET is_valid_move TO TRUE
    SET next_room TO "Pantry closet"
ELSE IF current_room EQUALS "Pantry closet" AND direction_input EQUALS "west" THEN
    SET is_valid_move TO TRUE
    SET next_room TO "Kitchen"
ELSE
    SET is_valid_move TO FALSE


TODO 4: Describe what happens when the movement command is valid.
# Include the room update and player output.
IF is_valid_move EQUALS TRUE THEN
    SET current_room TO next_room
    OUTPUT "You successfully move to the " + current_room + "."


# TODO 5: Describe what happens when the movement command is invalid.
# Include the output the player should receive.
IF is_valid_move EQUALS FALSE THEN
    OUTPUT "You cannot go that way! Your messy house blocks that path. Please choose a valid direction."


# TODO 6: Show how movement fits into repeated gameplay.
# The final game continues accepting commands until a required ending occurs.
WHILE player has not chosen to exit DO
    CALL prompt for movement command (TODO 2)
    CALL validate movement (TODO 3)
    IF valid THEN update room (TODO 4) ELSE display error (TODO 5)

